\begin{rSection}{Projects}



{\section*{\normalfont{ZKXCB} \hfill \textit{8/2024 - 11/2024}}}

ZKXCB is an application that allows users to anonymously review products on e-commerce platforms. The application leverages zero-knowledge proof technology and blockchain to ensure that transactions are transparent, secure, private, and anonymous.

\textbf{About project:}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Technologies Used: React.js, Node.js, Zero-Knowledge Proof, Consortium Blockchain, etc.
    \item Frameworks: Foundry (or Hardhat), Ethers.js (or Web3.js), ZK-SNARK, Hyperledger Besu, etc. 
\end{itemize}

\emph{Link:} \href{https://github.com/kientt265/-web3-zk-rating-e-comerce}{ZKXCB}
{\section*{\normalfont{ZKHealth} \hfill \textit{5/2024 - 7/2024}}}

ZKHealth is an application that allows patients to conceal sensitive personal information when receiving medical treatment at hospitals. The application utilizes zero-knowledge proof technology and consortium blockchain to ensure that only those involved in the treatment process can access the patient's information.

\textbf{About project:}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Technologies Used: React.js, Zero-Knowledge Proof, Blockchain, etc. 
    \item Frameworks:Technologies Used: React.js, Zero-Knowledge Proof, Blockchain, etc.  
\end{itemize}

\emph{Link:} \href{https://github.com/kientt265/-web3-zk-hopital}{ZKHealth}
{\section*{\normalfont{NFT Marketplace} \hfill \textit{2/2024 - 4/2024}}}

An NFT marketplace built on Solana, enabling users to mint, trade, list, and purchase NFTs
 securely and efficiently

\textbf{About project:}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Technologies Used: React.js, Node.js, Blockchain, etc. 
    \item Frameworks: Anchor, Web3.js, etc.  
\end{itemize}

\emph{Link:} \href{https://github.com/kientt265/nft_marketplace_solana}{NFT Marketplace}


